     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Ensured Vaccine Quality by installing remote data loggers in 7,000 vaccine storages that connect with SMILE application
- Expanding and improving a real-time vaccination logistics and monitoring system through SMILE
- Human resource capacities for the SMILE system are strengthened</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">S1 Progress: 
- 619 loggers have been installed and the remaining are in procurement
- More than 12,000 health workers trained to use SMILE for routine immunization and COVID-19 vaccination
- Recruited 20 SMILE operator manager and 5 Helpdesk
- Updated SMILE e-learning website on guidelines, quick guides
- SMILE dashboard has been updated simultaneously and equipped with new features, such as Stock Opname, Reconsilliation, Reporting, etc.
S2 Progress: 
- SMILE is on the scale-up to cover 514 districts and 34 provinces across the nation as requested by the MoH. SMILE also currently serves as the data backbone immunization program in Directorate General of Communicable Diseases (P2P)
- Integration of SMILE and ASIK data (Aplikasi Sehat IndonesiaKu; an individual registry for medical records) 
- Feasibility study of integration of pharmaceuticals and medical supplies into SMILE as requested by the Ministry of Health</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
